maria_sales: Quick heads-up — ACME Retail asked for a 1-week POC. Key asks: streaming SDK demo with function/tool calling, structured JSON outputs (order extraction), SAML SSO proof, and a rough price for reserved capacity. Can we support next-Wed kickoff? :eyes:

jamal_se: Sounds doable. Do we know expected QPS, payload size, and whether they need guaranteed capacity (Dedicated) vs hosted? Also any compliance must-haves?

maria_sales: They want guaranteed latency for POS lookups during peak traffic (approx 150 qps peak), and will likely require Dedicated for SLAs. Compliance: SOC2 + customer-supplied security questionnaire.

alex_devx: I can provision a dedicated POC cluster in us-west and give a temporary API key. For streaming + function calls we have a Node SDK example — can demo structured output via function calling to enforce JSON schema. Will need the ACME account alias and preferred region.

sara_security: Noted. We'll need to provide SOC2 summary and a completed security questionnaire. ACME also asked about pen-test history and encryption-in-transit/key mgmt. Link to our standard questionnaire: https://redwood.example.com/security/questionnaire (internal). I'll take point on the security doc; please send their version when you have it.

li_engineer: Pushing a short streaming example for the Node SDK (will use function-call pattern to emit structured JSON). Use this skeleton for the demo:```js
const stream = client.responses.stream({
  model: 'redwood-mini-1',
  input: 'Extract orders from this text',
  functions: [
    {
      name: 'extract_orders',
      parameters: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          order_id: { type: 'string' },
          items: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object' } },
          total: { type: 'number' }
        },
        required: ['order_id', 'items']
      }
    }
  ]
});

stream.on('data', (evt) => {
  // evt may include partial tokens, function call info, or final structured payload
  console.log(evt);
});
stream.on('end', () => console.log('done'));
```

li_engineer: For POC perf tips — enable prefix caching for repeated user prompts, set batch window to 5-10ms for throughput, and test with kv-cache enabled if they have long chat context. Quantization: recommend int8 for cost testing, but show float16 baseline for quality.

jamal_se: On pricing — for a short POC we can offer a trial Dedicated pool with a time-limited credit. For production reserved capacity, pricing beats on-hosted only at predictable heavy QPS; I'll draft a ballpark and sync with finance.

maria_sales: ACME also needs SAML SSO + SCIM so they can provision service accounts. Is that supported in Dedicated?

alex_devx: Yes — Dedicated supports SAML SSO with SCIM provisioning. I'll attach a sample SP metadata and a minimal config snippet in a follow-up DM.

opsbot: deploy-bot: dedicated-poc-us-west allocated to project/acme-retail (id: poc-acme-772) :white_check_mark:

maria_sales: Perfect — Jamal can you schedule kickoff Wed 10am PT? I'll send ACME the security questionnaire and ask for their SAML metadata and expected QPS profile.

jamal_se: Scheduled. I'll create a runbook for the demo (streaming ingest -> function calls -> output validation) and include a small load test script.

sara_security: I'll fill sections A1-A5 by Tue EOD and confirm encryption-at-rest keys (we use KMS). If they request an HSM path, flag and we'll engage infra.

li_engineer: One more note: when we demo structured output, show a failing schema case (invalid field) so we can highlight automatic validation and fallback to plain text for robustness.

maria_sales: Great work team. Next steps: Jamal kickoff Wed 10am PT, Alex provide creds and SP metadata, Sara complete questionnaire Tue EOD. :thumbsup:
